      en: "Palu-Mägi is a hill in northern Estonia, 8 km southeast of Tallinn. Rising to 45 meters, it is part of the Tallinn uplands. The name means 'Ash Hill' (palu = ash tree). The hill is wooded with ash and elm. Geologically, it consists of Cambrian claystone capped by glacial till. An 18th-century watchtower stands at the summit, now used as an observation tower. The hill is a popular recreational area for Tallinn residents.",
